<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.claude.devserver-gc — the SCHEDULED idle-reaper for per-worktree `next dev` servers.

  Measured 2026-08-07: 4 concurrent next-server processes holding 6.2 GB, with no reaper, cap or
  census anywhere in scripts/ bin/ hooks/. A commit gate is transient and self-terminating; a dev
  server is a permanent per-worktree allocation nobody collects.

  HOURLY, not daily. Unlike worktree-gc (whose subject is a directory that costs nothing to leave
  lying around overnight), the subject here is RESIDENT MEMORY on a box that has taken four kernel
  panics from compressor-segment exhaustion. A daily sweep would let a whole day's abandoned servers
  accumulate. The 30-minute birth grace inside devserver-census.sh is what keeps an hourly cadence
  from ever meeting a young server.

  :40 past the hour — off both worktree-gc (04:15) and reso's reaper (03:15), so no sweep is reading
  a process table another sweep is actively changing.

  ARMED 2026-08-10 (operator ratification "ratify all except cold-compile", decision packet
  99637eaee7b9): DEVGC_ACT=1 exported below, so the runner takes its real-reap branch. It shipped
  OBSERVE-ONLY BY DEFAULT (no DEVGC_ACT ⇒ `--dry-run`: logs which servers it WOULD reap, kills
  nothing) because arming an unattended process that kills running dev servers is the operator's
  decision, not an agent's — that decision has now been made and recorded. Dry-run evidence before
  arming: clean (keeps live-owner servers; would have reaped the ownerless spawner at 03:40 on
  2026-08-09, 27 min before that night's second storm). (Same split as
  com.claude.compressor-sentinel, whose CC_SENTINEL_ACT was likewise armed 2026-08-09.)

  `bash -c` (not a bare ProgramArguments path) because launchd expands neither ~ nor $HOME inside
  ProgramArguments. Standard*Path cannot take $HOME at all, hence the literals. The runner hardens
  its own PATH on line 1 — including /usr/sbin, where lsof lives and whose omission made reso's
  reaper blind to live sessions and reap one (2026-06-19).

  RunAtLoad false: a login is exactly when dev servers are most likely to be about to be used.

  C10: the OPERATOR loads this, via docs/activation/pending-activation/33-devserver-gc-activate.sh.
  Kill switch (no unload needed): touch ~/.claude/autonomy/devserver-gc.disabled
  Full stop:                      launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.claude.devserver-gc
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.claude.devserver-gc</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>export DEVGC_ACT=1; exec "$HOME/.claude/scripts/devserver-gc-run.sh"</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>40</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>LowPriorityIO</key>
    <true/>

    <key>Nice</key>
    <integer>10</integer>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/logs/devserver-gc.out.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/logs/devserver-gc.out.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
